## Grafana

Grafana is provisioned with:

- datasource: VictoriaMetrics
- dashboards:
{{- if .ProjectComponents.Cache }}
  - Cache Overview
{{- end }}
{{- if .ProjectComponents.Storage }}
  - Storage Overview
{{- end }}
{{- if .ProjectComponents.Events }}
  - Events Overview
{{- end }}
  - Auth Overview
{{- if .Components.Mail }}
  - Mail Overview
{{- end }}
  - HTTP Overview
{{- if .Components.HasDatabase }}
  - Database Overview
{{- end }}
{{- if .ProjectComponents.Jobs }}
  - Queue Overview
{{- end }}
{{- if .Components.Scheduler }}
  - Scheduler Overview
{{- end }}
- starred dashboards: generated overviews are starred automatically for the default admin user
- home dashboard: Platform Overview

The dashboards are authored against GoForj's metric contract rather than generic third-party dashboard imports.

Every generated dashboard includes an App filter backed by the emitted `app` metric label. Primitive dashboards also include filters for named accessors when applicable.

{{- if .ProjectComponents.Cache }}
- Cache Overview can be filtered to one named cache.
{{- end }}
{{- if .ProjectComponents.Storage }}
- Storage Overview can be filtered to one disk.
{{- end }}
{{- if .ProjectComponents.HasDatabase }}
- Database Overview can be filtered to one connection or table.
{{- end }}

If rendered dashboards do not refresh immediately:

1. Re-render the project with `forj render`.
2. Rebuild Grafana, then rerun the one-shot seeder explicitly:
   - `docker-compose up -d --build grafana`
   - `docker-compose run --rm --no-deps grafana-seed`
3. Wait for Grafana provisioning to rescan dashboards.
{{- end }}

## Querying

Use Grafana Explore or the VictoriaMetrics query UI to inspect raw metrics. Common production queries and the emitted metric families are documented in `internal/metrics/README.md`.

The most useful query dimensions are:

- `app`: which App composition app emitted the metric, such as `app`, `admin`, or `statuspage`.
- `source`: which logical source emitted the metric.
- `process`: which scrape target exposed the metric.
- `release`: the optional operator-facing release version attached by the scrape target.
- `revision`: the optional immutable source or artifact revision attached by the scrape target.
{{- if .ProjectComponents.Cache }}
- `cache`: which named cache handled the work.
{{- end }}
- `mailer` and `connection`: which named primitive handled the work.
{{- if .ProjectComponents.Storage }}
- `disk`: which named storage disk handled the work.
{{- end }}
{{- if .ProjectComponents.Jobs }}
- `queue`: which named queue handled the work.
{{- end }}
{{- if .ProjectComponents.Events }}
- `topic`, `handler`, and `bus`: which event path handled the work.
{{- end }}
- `route`, `method`, `status`: which HTTP route and outcome generated traffic.
- `job_name`, `target_kind`: which named unit of background work ran.
{{- if .ProjectComponents.Events }}
- `topic`, `handler`: which event topic or subscriber handled work.
{{- end }}

## Production Notes

- The rendered stack is optimized for local development and production-like troubleshooting.
- In Kubernetes, scrape each pod/process and let the metrics backend aggregate by label.
- Keep labels bounded. Do not add user IDs, emails, cache keys, raw URLs, raw SQL, request IDs, or arbitrary error strings as labels.
{{- if .Components.Grafana }}
- Change `GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD` before exposing Grafana outside local development.
{{- end }}
